From 32b1b18cb3e20583cec6d05402c6c63886526263 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:54:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(items): allow food use on Bedrock Peaceful difficulty

Allow the local consumable predicate to ignore hunger on a Bedrock client
in Peaceful difficulty. Retain the ordinary Java predicate and each food's
always-edible flag. Read current level difficulty on every use, including
connections translated remotely through ViaProxy.

Official Bedrock 1.26.60.5/BDS 1.26.60.6 protocol-2225 bread controls refuse
full-hunger use on Normal, consume one item after switching to Peaceful,
and refuse after switching back. The previous installed client never
enters use on Peaceful and retains all 16 items. Keep inventory consumption
and completion owned by the server; this hook only admits the local cycle.

DataDriven apple admission at full hunger differs independently from its
advertised component and remains separate native investigation. These
controls do not close the original intermittent food-use report.
---
 .../mixin/features/item/MixinConsumable.java  | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../viafabricplus-bedrock.mixins.json         |  1 +
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/item/MixinConsumable.java

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/item/MixinConsumable.java b/src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/item/MixinConsumable.java
